The Switch:

Interfaces Fast Ethernet 05 to 24 are shutdown. This prevents unnecessary doors from being open to attack by 
limiting unauthorised network connections.

VLAN MANAGEMENT

End devices are split into VLAN 10 and VLAN 20. This prevents end devices between the VLANs from communicating.

PC 1 - 192.168.10.11
PC 2 - 192.168.10.12
Laptop 1 - 192.168.20.11
Laptop 2 - 192.168.20.12

The PCs can communicate with each other. Likewise, the Laptops can communicate with each other. But a PC cant successfully
ping to laptop 1 as the resources are controlled i.e. a printer in vlan 10 can only be accessed by PCs in vlan 10.

NETWORK CONNECTIVITY

PC 1 and 2 can successfully ping to 192.168.10.1, as the assigned ip address for VLAN 10
Laptop 1 and 2 can successfully ping to 192.168.20.1, as the assigned ip address for VLAN 20

The Router:

Interfaces G0/1 is shutdown. This is unnecessary and thus hardens the router by reducing the attack surface.

VLAN MANAGEMENT

802.1q encapsulation is implemented for subinterfaces G0/0.10 and G0/0.20. For security purposes, 802.1q helps by:
- supporting the switchport mode trunks for routing traffic to VLAN 10 and 20.
- allowing a single trunk link to carry traffic for many VLANs
